      "content": "That's a pretty bleak outlook. I've heard some people argue that UBI actually acts as a floor that allows people to take more entrepreneurial risks or pursue education, which they say builds a more skilled workforce in the long run. Is there any actual economic data to support those kinds of positive outcomes, or is that just wishful thinking from the proponents?",
